# Security baseline

Treat every request, upload, and Gemini prompt as untrusted.

## Must enforce

- **AuthN**: JWT verified; check revocation; reject inactive users.
- **AuthZ**: Role checks on every mutating route; object-level checks (own resource / employer’s job).
- **Secrets**: Only via env / secret manager; never commit `.env` with real keys. Never print, quote, or echo secret values in chat, logs, or commits (see `secrets-and-sensitive-data` rule).
- **Uploads**: Type, size, and content checks; store outside web root; unique names.
- **AI**: Fence untrusted text; never execute model output; validate JSON with schemas.
- **PII**: Email/phone only to authorized viewers; public profiles strip contact by default.
- **Rate limits**: Assessments, login, upload, and AI endpoints need limits (app or gateway).

## Known product surfaces to harden

Auth, CV upload/analyze, assessments/submit, job apply, admin user/role changes, leaderboard PII.

## When implementing or reviewing

Run or follow `.cursor/skills/company-production-gate` / quality MCP tools. Report gaps as Critical / High / Medium / Low with a concrete fix — never “looks fine” without evidence.
